  (2, 145, $d$Attempting to look upon this weapon is like gazing into Oblivion itself - not
only does this mace seem to avoid light, upon closer inspection you realize
it's actively devouring the light around itself.  A palpable evil radiates from
the mace, yet it seems to be kept in check by something much greater.  Perhaps
this weapon is a tangible example of the old adage of fighting fire with fire.
What better way to destroy darkness than with darkness itself?$d$, $d$Attempting to look upon this weapon is like gazing into Oblivion itself - not
only does this mace seem to avoid light, upon closer inspection you realize
it's actively devouring the light around itself.  A palpable evil radiates from
the mace, yet it seems to be kept in check by something much greater.  Perhaps
