  (2, 147, $d$A long filigreed wooden handle connects to a wide, spiked ring of mythril.
Contained within the ring is an orb of ethereal flame, pale green, casting
wildly dancing shadows about.  The entire weapon phases in and out of existence
with the flickering flame, seemingly caught between this world and the next.
It is part of both worlds, yet truly of neither.  That tenuous connection makes
it ideal for breaking the bonds of things unnaturally tied to one world or the
other.$d$, $d$A long filigreed wooden handle connects to a wide, spiked ring of mythril.
