to anyone who knows the customs of Odaishyozen: it's meant to be worn in the
same way as a kimono.  Because it's made of cotton rather than silk and
designed for more casual wear, this style of robe is called a yukata.  It was
probably designed by someone from the resort who visited the Emerald Isle.$d$, $d$This light blue robe is decorated with a feather pattern, identifying it as
