  (237, 72, $d$   A long oval mirror set horizontal rather than the customary alignment of
vertical flashes continuously with images of this plane and others.  Cities
past and present vie with images of volcanoes, whirlpools, tornadoes and other
places of heavy activity, be it mortal or natural in nature.  The frame is a
work of art in itself: the scarlet silk that edges the mirror is embroidered
with golden runes of magic and slender outlines of fantastical creatures doing
battle.  Its value alone would be worth the price of a soul.$d$, $d$   A long oval mirror set horizontal rather than the customary alignment of
vertical flashes continuously with images of this plane and others.  Cities
past and present vie with images of volcanoes, whirlpools, tornadoes and other
places of heavy activity, be it mortal or natural in nature.  The frame is a
work of art in itself: the scarlet silk that edges the mirror is embroidered
with golden runes of magic and slender outlines of fantastical creatures doing
battle.  Its value alone would be worth the price of a soul.$d$),
  (237, 73, $d$Nearly two meters long, the koto resembles a zither.  It has thirteen strings,
each witha moveable bridge to adjust the pitch to the musician's desired tone.
It is played with three picks: one each on the thumb, forefinger, and middle
finger and has a thin, almost ghostly quality.  Many of the haunting melodies
played on the koto bring with them images of a solitary green island, isolated
from the rest of the world but holding its own beauty.$d$, $d$Nearly two meters long, the koto resembles a zither.  It has thirteen strings,
each witha moveable bridge to adjust the pitch to the musician's desired tone.
