  (238, 10, $d$Made of a rough, heavy silk, the cloak is a tan color lined in white and,
judging by the way the fabric drapes, would sweep out impressively behind
anyone wearing it.  The dragon symbol is set in the center of the back, showing
a pale dragon done in metallic thread shimmering in the light, standing rampant
with a five-taloned foot raised as if in greeting.  The dragon looks, as
dragons tend to, extremely fierce.  Inside the collar in gray thread is the
maker's mark stitched into the fabric, but it is faint enough that it cannot be
read.$d$, $d$Made of a rough, heavy silk, the cloak is a tan color lined in white and,
judging by the way the fabric drapes, would sweep out impressively behind
