  (238, 17, $d$A bowl made of a blackened metal inlaid with silver sits here.  Inside it are
smudge marks that smell faint but sweet, probably from incense.  The silver
forms intricate knotwork shapes, some tarnished but others bright.  At the
bottom is the symbol of a raven with wings outstretched outlined in silver with
feathers and talons marked with thinner lines than the rest of the inlay.$d$, $d$A bowl made of a blackened metal inlaid with silver sits here.  Inside it are
