  (238, 93, $d$Curving gracefully from hilt to tip, this cutlass is a work of art.  Its
flaring guard is inlaid with silver skulls so that the poor soul at the
receiving end can see his macabre demise before meeting his fate.  Razor-sharp
and very dangerous-looking, it would probably cut through a normal pirate sash
if its owner were not careful.  The hilt is set with a large black diamond, and
looking closely into the depths of the gem you can see the blurry shape of
letters, forming the word "Dakhod".$d$, $d$Curving gracefully from hilt to tip, this cutlass is a work of art.  Its
