Butchery, so he may watch every kill up close.$d$),
  (462, 3, $d$Named for the Demon Lord Yeenoghu's holy weapon, this massive and deadly triple
flail is not in fact the real artifact, though it is an impressive replica and
still extremely potent.  Weapons such as these are carried by Fangs of
Yeenoghu, warrior-shamans imbued directly with a demonic spirit by Yeenoghu
himself.  This one has three spike-headed orbs dangling from long chains,
attached to a sturdy haft.  A bulging eye is drawn on each orb in blood, an
invocation of Yeenoghu to watch the butchery committed in his name.$d$, $d$Named for the Demon Lord Yeenoghu's holy weapon, this massive and deadly triple
