  (464, 0, $d$     This beautiful fountain appears to have been carved from a single block of
marble, rather amazing as it stands about twice your height and three times
that wide.  A series of basins carry water down the sides as they fill and
overflow, the glistening liquid eventually running out a large sluice on the
western side where the vast volume of water becomes a swift brook.
     All manner of the aviary's winged species wing about in the flowing water,
splashing the life-giving fluid all about as they make fun of the simple task
of bathing on this warm afternoon.  So many of the brilliantly-plumed creatures
light upon the marble basins that the fountain looks more a floral arrangement
than a sculpture.  Perhaps you wondered at first about the plainness of the
white marble, but as a backdrop for the avians it makes a perfect picture.
     Carved into the side of the fountain nearest you is some kind of
inscription, though you'd need to take a closer look to make out what the
letters say.  Just below the inscription is a circular carving of a beautiful
woman set bas-relief in the gleaming white stone.$d$, $d$     This beautiful fountain appears to have been carved from a single block of
marble, rather amazing as it stands about twice your height and three times
that wide.  A series of basins carry water down the sides as they fill and
overflow, the glistening liquid eventually running out a large sluice on the
western side where the vast volume of water becomes a swift brook.
     All manner of the aviary's winged species wing about in the flowing water,
splashing the life-giving fluid all about as they make fun of the simple task
