woman set bas-relief in the gleaming white stone.$d$),
  (464, 1, $d$Long yellow and grey feathers make up this piece of stylish headwear.  Upon the
pate of some hapless bird it must have been beautifully expressive, as the
crest itself would swing up or lie back against the bird's head to express
interest, excitement, fear, and love.  Holding the feathered garment in your
hands, you cannot help but feel sorry for the bird and wonder if you might be
able to recreate even a degree of its vitality.$d$, $d$Long yellow and grey feathers make up this piece of stylish headwear.  Upon the
pate of some hapless bird it must have been beautifully expressive, as the
crest itself would swing up or lie back against the bird's head to express
interest, excitement, fear, and love.  Holding the feathered garment in your
hands, you cannot help but feel sorry for the bird and wonder if you might be
able to recreate even a degree of its vitality.$d$),
  (464, 2, $d$     Baked apparently from grains harvested within the aviary itself, this loaf
of bread is coarse and rather crude, but certainly looks appetizing to the
empty of stomach.  Breaking the dark brown loaf open, there are quite a few
whole kernels and seeds of grain still intact, and the flour certainly was
barely crushed and sifted.  Perhaps this bread was intended as more of a treat
for the birds above than for human consumption.$d$, $d$     Baked apparently from grains harvested within the aviary itself, this loaf
of bread is coarse and rather crude, but certainly looks appetizing to the
empty of stomach.  Breaking the dark brown loaf open, there are quite a few
whole kernels and seeds of grain still intact, and the flour certainly was
barely crushed and sifted.  Perhaps this bread was intended as more of a treat
for the birds above than for human consumption.$d$),
  (464, 3, $d$Though not exactly industrial-sized, these garden shears have a wickedly- sharp
serrated edge to their blades and a handle that feels warm and heavy in your
palm.  Certainly they could clip through the most stubborn of dragon- shaped
shrubbery and perhaps even be turned to more gruesome ends - wouldn't those
blades do a number on someone's arm or fingers, and wouldn't it be something to
see the metal handles protruding from the back of yon adventurer?  Indeed, the
shears make for a nasty weapon.

There is an inscription of some sort along the handle.$d$, $d$Though not exactly industrial-sized, these garden shears have a wickedly- sharp
