  (464, 5, $d$The beak of a parrot, this grey hook-shaped bill has razor-sharp edges honed
daily by its former owner.  Though most birds are not aggressive, only the most
foolhardy would not look to its own defense.  It looks as if someone has
drilled two holes in the sides of the beak and run a leather thong through them
so that you could tie the hookbill onto your head; it might also function well
as a kind of dagger in hand.$d$, $d$The beak of a parrot, this grey hook-shaped bill has razor-sharp edges honed
