  (464, 7, $d$Yech!  Though the birds within the aviary's walls are far from domesticated -
much less housebroken - happening upon such a nasty bit of droppings is an
unpleasant surprise; generally the aviary grounds crew seem to do a pretty good
job keeping the paths clean, turning such offal into the soil to act as
fertilizer for the exotic plant life.

The core of the droppings is a greenish-grey snakelike solid, surrounded by an
off-white liquid that is quickly drying in the sun.  Though bird droppings do
not have the disgusting smell of other animal feces, they are still rather
repulsive nonetheless.$d$, $d$Yech!  Though the birds within the aviary's walls are far from domesticated -
