  (464, 8, $d$     A slender brown stem supports a wide blossom of tiny seeds, giving the
millet spray the appearance of a cat's tail even down to the fuzzy filaments
growing all about the seeds much like tiny hairs.  Though perhaps the millet
does not look all that appetizing to you, to birds it is a treat on par with
ice cream and other unhealthy sweets.  Many a feathered flier can be seen about
the aviary picking away at the tiny but tasty seeds well into the evening
hours.$d$, $d$     A slender brown stem supports a wide blossom of tiny seeds, giving the
millet spray the appearance of a cat's tail even down to the fuzzy filaments
growing all about the seeds much like tiny hairs.  Though perhaps the millet
does not look all that appetizing to you, to birds it is a treat on par with
ice cream and other unhealthy sweets.  Many a feathered flier can be seen about
the aviary picking away at the tiny but tasty seeds well into the evening
