  (464, 10, $d$     Once a feather is completely grown and mature it is like human hair - dead
and unfeeling.  However, as they grow in, a bird's feathers have their own
blood supply and can indeed feel pain.  Occasionally something happens to cause
a bird to break or otherwise lose one of these bloodfeathers.
     Other than the dark vein of red down its center and its broken, uneven
end, this feather seems like any other.  Whatever bird lost it must have had
spectacular yellow and blue plumage... but what good is it to you?$d$, $d$     Once a feather is completely grown and mature it is like human hair - dead
and unfeeling.  However, as they grow in, a bird's feathers have their own
blood supply and can indeed feel pain.  Occasionally something happens to cause
a bird to break or otherwise lose one of these bloodfeathers.
     Other than the dark vein of red down its center and its broken, uneven
end, this feather seems like any other.  Whatever bird lost it must have had
spectacular yellow and blue plumage... but what good is it to you?$d$),
  (464, 11, $d$Made of a thin, stretchy material lined with a warm layer of fuzzy down, these
sleeves would be perfect for keeping your arms warm beneath your overcoat.
However, the thin material would provide little benefit for warriors and might
seem even a bit sissified for the more beastly of occupations.  The thin
material has enough stretch to it that you might even be able to wear the
sleeves about your legs like a pair of tights in a stretch (no pun intended!
)$d$, $d$Made of a thin, stretchy material lined with a warm layer of fuzzy down, these
