  (488, 56, $d$You see a key fit for a small child-- larger than most keys, simplistic
in design, and strung on a pretty red ribbon, so its wearer would be sure
not to lose it.$d$, $d$You see a key fit for a small child-- larger than most keys, simplistic
in design, and strung on a pretty red ribbon, so its wearer would be sure
not to lose it.$d$),
  (489, 1, $d$The bronze staff in your hands is huge-- it's almost too large to hold
effectively.  It pulses with power, its gemstone decorations lit as if from
some inner radiance.  A crystal on its tip sparkles with light.  Your hands
tingle at contact with it.  You wonder what it does.$d$, $d$The bronze staff in your hands is huge-- it's almost too large to hold
effectively.  It pulses with power, its gemstone decorations lit as if from
some inner radiance.  A crystal on its tip sparkles with light.  Your hands
tingle at contact with it.  You wonder what it does.$d$),
  (489, 2, $d$Your hand aches to wield this fabulous sword. Made of pure white steel,
glowing as if from some inner light, it pulses like the heart of legend
itself. This is the sword of the ancient heroes out of your land's
stories, the sword that destroyed armies almost of its own accord. This
is the sword of the god Lokari. It's lavishly decorated: an ivy-leaf
pattern along the blade. The quillons are short, but curved upward in a
continuation of that pattern, making a very effective looking basket
hilt. A huge onyx forms the pommel. You can detect in this amazing sword
that touch of greatness that has made its name revered -- and feared --
by all great warriors.
f/$d$, $d$Your hand aches to wield this fabulous sword. Made of pure white steel,
