cloak isn't quite what it seems.  It seems to have a sense of power to it.
Some sense of intuition you didn't even know you had tells you to handle this
cloak carefully.$d$),
  (489, 7, $d$This is the Cailaran Vest, which you've heard of in stories, seen in tapestries
and paintings, even idly imagined seeking (and finding).  It's a long green
vest, belted around the waist with a bronze clasp, and flowing to the calves.
The grass-green silk is lightly embroidered in golden thread in a criss-cross
pattern.  The double-breasted collar is embroidered as well, in golden
four-pointed stars.  It'd look perfect with a silk blouse and breeches.$d$, $d$This is the Cailaran Vest, which you've heard of in stories, seen in tapestries
and paintings, even idly imagined seeking (and finding).  It's a long green
vest, belted around the waist with a bronze clasp, and flowing to the calves.
The grass-green silk is lightly embroidered in golden thread in a criss-cross
pattern.  The double-breasted collar is embroidered as well, in golden
four-pointed stars.  It'd look perfect with a silk blouse and breeches.$d$),
  (489, 8, $d$Here you see Rahmat, the ancient sword used by the High Paladin of the
Order of the Sun. Its blue steel blade gleams as though it were brand
new, not older than the mountains, its edge sharp as Truth. Its hilt is a
silvery metal, with claw quillions. A brilliant green emerald forms its
pommel. You sense that only someone truly Good, and truly strong, could
wield this weapon.$d$, $d$Here you see Rahmat, the ancient sword used by the High Paladin of the
Order of the Sun. Its blue steel blade gleams as though it were brand
