  (489, 13, $d$You see a small pendant on a chain. Further investigation reveals that
the pendant is actually a locket, inscribed with a pentagram. The
delicate golden chain seems barely strong enough to support the meager
weight of the locket. You cannot pry the locket open, though. You wonder
why. It's pretty old. Perhaps it's just stuck closed. Whatever the
reason, you take an instant dislike to the locket. You're quite sure it's
going to be nothing but bad news.$d$, $d$You see a small pendant on a chain. Further investigation reveals that
