  (489, 20, $d$And now... The end of the quest. Here you see the goal you have fought
for, and won. Dare you open it, to claim the prize within? Ah, but the
carved and scrollworked swordcase is locked? You lean in to look closer,
but see only crayon marks at the bottom of the wooden case -- marks that
make no sense to you. Perhaps some wizard laid a curse upon it, so it
would open only with a key of the caster's choosing...$d$, $d$And now... The end of the quest. Here you see the goal you have fought
