  (533, 19, $d$The fountain is essentially a low circular wall that contains a small
pool of ice-cold water.  In the center of the pool - rising out of it -
is a small dragon, its head raised toward the sky.  Water gently flows
out of its open mouth.  Considering the temperature in this cavern you are
amazed that the water has not frozen.  A plaque affixed to the base of the
fountain reads, "Water Bringeth Life."$d$, $d$The fountain is essentially a low circular wall that contains a small
pool of ice-cold water.  In the center of the pool - rising out of it -
is a small dragon, its head raised toward the sky.  Water gently flows
out of its open mouth.  Considering the temperature in this cavern you are
amazed that the water has not frozen.  A plaque affixed to the base of the
fountain reads, "Water Bringeth Life."$d$),
  (533, 20, $d$As you look at the large white dragon's egg you seem to remember something
