  (564, 7, $d$The dagger has four separate blades that stem out from the handle.  Each of the
blades are extremely sharp and jagged shaped.$d$, $d$The dagger has four separate blades that stem out from the handle.  Each of the
blades are extremely sharp and jagged shaped.$d$),
  (580, 1, $d$It is a long, single-bladed sword that has a slightly curved blade and a short,
octagonal crossguard.  The blade has a wavy, rippled coloration along its
insanely sharp edge.  Its hilt is enamelled black wood wrapped with black silk
cord.$d$, $d$It is a long, single-bladed sword that has a slightly curved blade and a short,
octagonal crossguard.  The blade has a wavy, rippled coloration along its
insanely sharp edge.  Its hilt is enamelled black wood wrapped with black silk
cord.$d$),
  (580, 2, $d$The bottle is white ceramic, painted with blue symbols and pictures you
can't read or identify. It looks like it could hold a lot of liquid.$d$, $d$The bottle is white ceramic, painted with blue symbols and pictures you
can't read or identify. It looks like it could hold a lot of liquid.$d$),
  (580, 3, $d$How can this be?  You can feel that this entire sword is made of paper, yet
somehow it's hard as steel, and somehow it has an edge that cuts your finger
when you test it!$d$, $d$How can this be?  You can feel that this entire sword is made of paper, yet
somehow it's hard as steel, and somehow it has an edge that cuts your finger
when you test it!$d$),
  (580, 4, $d$The plain, light brown clay of the bowl is finely worked, but unornamented.
You can see fine worksmanship in it, but you can't imagine why anyone would
want one of these.$d$, $d$The plain, light brown clay of the bowl is finely worked, but unornamented.
You can see fine worksmanship in it, but you can't imagine why anyone would
want one of these.$d$),
  (580, 5, $d$The necklace is made of several very large, flawless panels of jade.  You run
your fingers over the smooth stone and can feel supernatural power contained
inside this rare piece of art.$d$, $d$The necklace is made of several very large, flawless panels of jade.  You run
your fingers over the smooth stone and can feel supernatural power contained
inside this rare piece of art.$d$),
  (580, 6, $d$The whisk is only as large as a woman's hand, and made of bamboo.  Several
pieces of light bamboo have been woven together at the handle, their ends
allowed to fray to form a whisk.  It's lightweight, and its whorled strands of
bamboo would make it an excellent whisk for the powdered tea of the tea
ceremony of Odaishyozen.$d$, $d$The whisk is only as large as a woman's hand, and made of bamboo.  Several
pieces of light bamboo have been woven together at the handle, their ends
allowed to fray to form a whisk.  It's lightweight, and its whorled strands of
bamboo would make it an excellent whisk for the powdered tea of the tea
ceremony of Odaishyozen.$d$),
  (580, 7, $d$This is a very simple length of black cloth, hemmed all around very
neatly. There's literally nothing impressive about it.$d$, $d$This is a very simple length of black cloth, hemmed all around very
neatly. There's literally nothing impressive about it.$d$),
  (580, 8, $d$The book almost hums with power.  You approach it reverently, ready to see the
face of some god in its pages, but then...  Then...  You feel its sheer evil
nature and realize this is not a text to praise a god, but entrap one!$d$, $d$The book almost hums with power.  You approach it reverently, ready to see the
face of some god in its pages, but then...  Then...  You feel its sheer evil
nature and realize this is not a text to praise a god, but entrap one!$d$),
  (580, 9, $d$The gold of this key has been cunningly worked with figures of majestic
birds. You wish you could actually see what inspired it!$d$, $d$The gold of this key has been cunningly worked with figures of majestic
birds. You wish you could actually see what inspired it!$d$),
  (580, 11, $d$As you whirl this beautiful silk kimono through the air, you are struck by how
light, airy, and altogether good-looking this garment is.  You've heard that
this gown has magical powers that turn its wearer beautiful, even irresistable.
Maybe you should wear it and see?$d$, $d$As you whirl this beautiful silk kimono through the air, you are struck by how
light, airy, and altogether good-looking this garment is.  You've heard that
this gown has magical powers that turn its wearer beautiful, even irresistable.
Maybe you should wear it and see?$d$),
  (580, 12, $d$The fan looks much more threatening than your run-of-the-mill fan!  For
starters, its rods are made of black-lacquered wood.  Instead of finely painted
rice paper over the rods, you see thick white cloth, with a golden ball painted
on both sides.  It could hang folded from your hand, and then, with a flick of
your wrist, it could extend, becoming quite a parrying device.$d$, $d$The fan looks much more threatening than your run-of-the-mill fan!  For
starters, its rods are made of black-lacquered wood.  Instead of finely painted
rice paper over the rods, you see thick white cloth, with a golden ball painted
on both sides.  It could hang folded from your hand, and then, with a flick of
your wrist, it could extend, becoming quite a parrying device.$d$),
  (580, 13, $d$The helmet is made of gold-plated steel, but it's very light. A pair of
thin, flat horns protrudes from the very middle of the helmet's front.$d$, $d$The helmet is made of gold-plated steel, but it's very light. A pair of
thin, flat horns protrudes from the very middle of the helmet's front.$d$),
  (580, 14, $d$This armor is so light that you wonder that it could be at all effective!
Made from strips of bamboo cleverly lashed together with wire, it covers from
the throat to the knees.  It looks like it ties in the back.$d$, $d$This armor is so light that you wonder that it could be at all effective!
Made from strips of bamboo cleverly lashed together with wire, it covers from
the throat to the knees.  It looks like it ties in the back.$d$),
  (580, 15, $d$It is a fine bracelet that looks like it was carved from one large pearl, with
a twisting whorled design inlaid with gold.  It fits over the wrist, sliding on
without a clasp or hinge.  It glows with the lustrous inner light that only the
finest pearls have.$d$, $d$It is a fine bracelet that looks like it was carved from one large pearl, with
a twisting whorled design inlaid with gold.  It fits over the wrist, sliding on
without a clasp or hinge.  It glows with the lustrous inner light that only the
finest pearls have.$d$),
  (580, 16, $d$The naginata (for that is what you heard this long spearlike scythe was once
called) is sharp-bladed and looks pretty nasty, but for all its ungainly size,
you can feel how quick a weapon it is.$d$, $d$The naginata (for that is what you heard this long spearlike scythe was once
called) is sharp-bladed and looks pretty nasty, but for all its ungainly size,
you can feel how quick a weapon it is.$d$),
  (580, 17, $d$The lute is seven-stringed, with a larger belly than you might expect of
such a light-sounding instrument. It is undecorated.$d$, $d$The lute is seven-stringed, with a larger belly than you might expect of
such a light-sounding instrument. It is undecorated.$d$),
  (580, 18, $d$The main body of this exquisite ring is made of bright silver that seems to
glow aquamarine-blue with an inner light.  The pearl that adorns it is stunning
and larger than usual, with deep blue sapphires running otter-swift around the
main center of attention.  The ring is neither wide nor narrow, making it
wearable by either men or women.$d$, $d$The main body of this exquisite ring is made of bright silver that seems to
glow aquamarine-blue with an inner light.  The pearl that adorns it is stunning
and larger than usual, with deep blue sapphires running otter-swift around the
main center of attention.  The ring is neither wide nor narrow, making it
wearable by either men or women.$d$),
  (580, 20, $d$You see a plain cream-colored ivory dagger, very simply carved, with a
leather-wrapped handle.  It has a good balance, but other than that, it's
nothing spectacular.$d$, $d$You see a plain cream-colored ivory dagger, very simply carved, with a
leather-wrapped handle.  It has a good balance, but other than that, it's
nothing spectacular.$d$),
  (580, 100, $d$Sleeves which fall only to the elbow mark this as a men's-style kimono, unlike
the full-sleeved women's kimono.  This way, the wearer still has plenty of room
to handle a weapon.  Made of fine silk, it is meant to be worn loosely to allow
even greater freedom of movement.  Understated in its elegance, any warrior
would wear this robe with pride.$d$, $d$Sleeves which fall only to the elbow mark this as a men's-style kimono, unlike
the full-sleeved women's kimono.  This way, the wearer still has plenty of room
to handle a weapon.  Made of fine silk, it is meant to be worn loosely to allow
even greater freedom of movement.  Understated in its elegance, any warrior
would wear this robe with pride.$d$),
  (580, 101, $d$So light it seems made out of cloud rather than fabric, the silk has been dyed
a dark blue and covered with dragonfly embroidery.  Looking closer, it seems
that the dark blue kimono is only the outermost of three layers - inside it are
a light blue and white kimono.  No wonder it can be used as armor!$d$, $d$So light it seems made out of cloud rather than fabric, the silk has been dyed
a dark blue and covered with dragonfly embroidery.  Looking closer, it seems
that the dark blue kimono is only the outermost of three layers - inside it are
a light blue and white kimono.  No wonder it can be used as armor!$d$),
  (580, 102, $d$A simple robe of orange silk, the kimono is so light and soft that it would
surely feel heavenly against the skin.  With the long, draping sleeves that
could be used to conceal any manner of things, this women's-style kimono is
tied with a much larger sash than the men's-style kimono are.$d$, $d$A simple robe of orange silk, the kimono is so light and soft that it would
surely feel heavenly against the skin.  With the long, draping sleeves that
could be used to conceal any manner of things, this women's-style kimono is
tied with a much larger sash than the men's-style kimono are.$d$),
  (580, 103, $d$Made of a raw, tan-colored silk that is much heavier than normal silk, the
kimono is patterned with leaves of red, yellow, orange, and brown.  The leaves
are embroidered on with silk thread, making them shine in the light.  The body
of the kimono must have been made of raw silk so that the textures, both
tactile and visual, would complement each other.  This robe is truly a work of
art.$d$, $d$Made of a raw, tan-colored silk that is much heavier than normal silk, the
kimono is patterned with leaves of red, yellow, orange, and brown.  The leaves
are embroidered on with silk thread, making them shine in the light.  The body
of the kimono must have been made of raw silk so that the textures, both
tactile and visual, would complement each other.  This robe is truly a work of
art.$d$),
  (580, 104, $d$Made of thin black cotton, this kimono blends in perfectly with the shadows of
night.  Silk would provide a telltale sheen, though it would also be lighter,
but the black-dyed cotton absorbs light rather than reflecting it.  It is
utterly silent, not even giving the usual "whoosh" of fabric when moved.  The
sleeves fall only to the elbows, providing plenty of room to swing a weapon.$d$, $d$Made of thin black cotton, this kimono blends in perfectly with the shadows of
night.  Silk would provide a telltale sheen, though it would also be lighter,
but the black-dyed cotton absorbs light rather than reflecting it.  It is
utterly silent, not even giving the usual "whoosh" of fabric when moved.  The
sleeves fall only to the elbows, providing plenty of room to swing a weapon.$d$),
  (580, 105, $d$This kimono is heavier than it looks!  Upon closer inspection, you see that it
is really made of not one but twelve separate layers, from a golden silk
embroidered with red on the outermost to a plain white cotton underkimono on
the lowest layer.  How do people move wearing this many layers of clothing?
It is a good thing the kimono is made to a loose-fitting design, or else they
wouldn't be able to.  Voluminous sleeves provide a hiding place for trinkets
and small, useful items without all that fuss about pockets.  Just being seen
in such a robe would surely elevate one's social status.$d$, $d$This kimono is heavier than it looks!  Upon closer inspection, you see that it
is really made of not one but twelve separate layers, from a golden silk
embroidered with red on the outermost to a plain white cotton underkimono on
the lowest layer.  How do people move wearing this many layers of clothing?
It is a good thing the kimono is made to a loose-fitting design, or else they
wouldn't be able to.  Voluminous sleeves provide a hiding place for trinkets
and small, useful items without all that fuss about pockets.  Just being seen
in such a robe would surely elevate one's social status.$d$),
  (580, 106, $d$   It is a beige-colored bamboo pen set with a brush tip that allows
it to be used for fine calligraphy in the Odaishyozen style. The
brush tip is made of soft black sable hair.$d$, $d$   It is a beige-colored bamboo pen set with a brush tip that allows
it to be used for fine calligraphy in the Odaishyozen style. The
brush tip is made of soft black sable hair.$d$),
  (580, 144, $d$Somehow this key has been carved out of solid opal. It glitters with
inner fire as you turn it this way and that.$d$, $d$Somehow this key has been carved out of solid opal. It glitters with
inner fire as you turn it this way and that.$d$),
  (580, 150, $d$This hunk of dried, smoked fish is salty but tender enough to
eat out of hand. It smells faintly of the sea, and is somewhat
reddish-brown in color.$d$, $d$This hunk of dried, smoked fish is salty but tender enough to
eat out of hand. It smells faintly of the sea, and is somewhat
reddish-brown in color.$d$),
  (580, 196, $d$The wood of this key is black and steel-hard. You try to break it, and
can't. You wonder what it opens.$d$, $d$The wood of this key is black and steel-hard. You try to break it, and
can't. You wonder what it opens.$d$),
  (580, 200, $d$This key is nothing special. It's plain, nondescript metal, completely
undecorated. It's almost rusted, in fact. You almost toss it aside, but
as you do, you hear a faint whisper, a woman's soft voice, pleading...$d$, $d$This key is nothing special. It's plain, nondescript metal, completely
undecorated. It's almost rusted, in fact. You almost toss it aside, but
as you do, you hear a faint whisper, a woman's soft voice, pleading...$d$),
  (583, 51, $d$This dress is made of fine satin; it's the color of orchids, with gold
braid accents and dark purple ribbon trim. The neckline seems a bit
daring, but from the cut of the dress, you can tell that whoever wears
this garment wouldn't be embarassed unduly by showing a bit of cleavage.$d$, $d$This dress is made of fine satin; it's the color of orchids, with gold
braid accents and dark purple ribbon trim. The neckline seems a bit
daring, but from the cut of the dress, you can tell that whoever wears
this garment wouldn't be embarassed unduly by showing a bit of cleavage.$d$),
  (583, 52, $d$You've never seen such a magnificent gown! It's good enough for a
princess or queen to wear to her nuptials, with a long, flowing skirt
of white silk tulle, and a bodice of the same and covered in handmade
laces from around the world. The leg-o-mutton sleeves end in triangles
of soft white fabric that partially cover the backs of the bride's hands.
Truly, it's a magnificent garment.$d$, $d$You've never seen such a magnificent gown! It's good enough for a
princess or queen to wear to her nuptials, with a long, flowing skirt
of white silk tulle, and a bodice of the same and covered in handmade
laces from around the world. The leg-o-mutton sleeves end in triangles
of soft white fabric that partially cover the backs of the bride's hands.
Truly, it's a magnificent garment.$d$),
  (583, 53, $d$What a dashing black suit this is! You just know that it would make
any man's physique appear perfect, through the cunning cut and elegant
flow of its dark silk fabric.$d$, $d$What a dashing black suit this is! You just know that it would make
any man's physique appear perfect, through the cunning cut and elegant
flow of its dark silk fabric.$d$),
  (583, 54, $d$The bouquet is made up of what must be a hundred absolutely perfect
roses. Most of them are cream colored, but there are a few golden
ones thrown in to add artistic flavor. The bouquet is very large,
going down to the bride's knees, but it's so light that she could
carry it easily.$d$, $d$The bouquet is made up of what must be a hundred absolutely perfect
roses. Most of them are cream colored, but there are a few golden
ones thrown in to add artistic flavor. The bouquet is very large,
going down to the bride's knees, but it's so light that she could
carry it easily.$d$),
  (583, 55, $d$This perfect orange flower's petals are soft as silk. It exudes a
strange, exotic fragrance that allures you, making you feel stronger,
and somehow more alert to any dangers around you.$d$, $d$This perfect orange flower's petals are soft as silk. It exudes a
strange, exotic fragrance that allures you, making you feel stronger,
and somehow more alert to any dangers around you.$d$),
  (583, 61, $d$Throwing you into a world of power and mystery, this hood has magic beyond
the understanding of mortal men. Given by the gods, it is truly a gift of
great value and it would be a poor idea to toss it aside. You have never
seen an artifact quite like this.$d$, $d$Throwing you into a world of power and mystery, this hood has magic beyond
the understanding of mortal men. Given by the gods, it is truly a gift of
great value and it would be a poor idea to toss it aside. You have never
seen an artifact quite like this.$d$),
  (583, 63, $d$This finely made mantle is made of dark green velvet, edged in thick
ermine fur. The dark spots stand out against the white fur, and both
are an excellent foil for the velvet, which is brocaded in gold.$d$, $d$This finely made mantle is made of dark green velvet, edged in thick
ermine fur. The dark spots stand out against the white fur, and both
are an excellent foil for the velvet, which is brocaded in gold.$d$),
  (583, 65, $d$This sheet seems a little threadbare, which is probably why it
isn't on somebody's bed. The little golden-and-green flowers
that adorn it are sprightly, although they detract from the
general image the wearer must be trying to project.$d$, $d$This sheet seems a little threadbare, which is probably why it
isn't on somebody's bed. The little golden-and-green flowers
that adorn it are sprightly, although they detract from the
general image the wearer must be trying to project.$d$),
  (583, 66, $d$This wreath is the mark of the true champion. It is given only
by the hand of a God or Goddess, and only for true merit. If
you have nobly won this wreath, wear it with pride. If you did
not earn it, expect to lose it.$d$, $d$This wreath is the mark of the true champion. It is given only
by the hand of a God or Goddess, and only for true merit. If
you have nobly won this wreath, wear it with pride. If you did
not earn it, expect to lose it.$d$),
  (584, 1, $d$This delicate golden feather is about as long as your forearm.  The long, lacy
fronds of the feather's plumage waft slightly in the breeze.  Oh, and it also
glows like the sun.  Just touching it makes your spirit soar!$d$, $d$This delicate golden feather is about as long as your forearm.  The long, lacy
fronds of the feather's plumage waft slightly in the breeze.  Oh, and it also
glows like the sun.  Just touching it makes your spirit soar!$d$),
  (584, 2, $d$You behold a very simple wooden box. The tiny slats of the fist-sized
container are made of poorly cured wood that is warped and cracked in
places. A richly patina'd bronze clasp fastens the box's lid shut.$d$, $d$You behold a very simple wooden box. The tiny slats of the fist-sized
container are made of poorly cured wood that is warped and cracked in
places. A richly patina'd bronze clasp fastens the box's lid shut.$d$),
  (584, 3, $d$This golden key is ornamented with small gems, but it's not very heavy or
even very complicated looking. Scratched into its surface, you see some
words scratched into its surface in a strange, runish script.$d$, $d$This golden key is ornamented with small gems, but it's not very heavy or
even very complicated looking. Scratched into its surface, you see some
words scratched into its surface in a strange, runish script.$d$),
  (584, 5, $d$This well, a pool of water edged in red-brown bricks, bubbles up from
beneath your feet. To drink from it, you must kneel on the bricks
carefully!$d$, $d$This well, a pool of water edged in red-brown bricks, bubbles up from
beneath your feet. To drink from it, you must kneel on the bricks
carefully!$d$),
  (584, 6, $d$This tambourine is made of two wooden discs pegged together.  Through the gaps
in between them, someone has thrust pairs of small brass circles.  The
slightest movement makes the circles jingle together, producing a wild,
mysterious cacophony.$d$, $d$This tambourine is made of two wooden discs pegged together.  Through the gaps
in between them, someone has thrust pairs of small brass circles.  The
slightest movement makes the circles jingle together, producing a wild,
mysterious cacophony.$d$),
  (584, 7, $d$It is written in ink that has gone brown with age on parchment that
is nearly yellow. The edges crumble as you read; you take special
care not to destroy this missive from the past. But it reads only:

      My beloved Arturio, please believe that I act only to protect
      you and Frederick. Remember the chants and spells I taught
      you and the rest of our family, and remember that yours is
      a rich heritage. Should you ever need the help of the Goddess
      Mielikki, you need only ask.

The letter has been folded and refolded many, many times.$d$, $d$It is written in ink that has gone brown with age on parchment that
is nearly yellow. The edges crumble as you read; you take special
care not to destroy this missive from the past. But it reads only:

      My beloved Arturio, please believe that I act only to protect
      you and Frederick. Remember the chants and spells I taught
      you and the rest of our family, and remember that yours is
      a rich heritage. Should you ever need the help of the Goddess
      Mielikki, you need only ask.

The letter has been folded and refolded many, many times.$d$),
  (584, 8, $d$You've never seen such exquisite goldworking.  This locket, on its whisper-thin
golden link necklace, seems very old.  The hinges on it are coming a bit loose,
but it's still pretty tightly closed.$d$, $d$You've never seen such exquisite goldworking.  This locket, on its whisper-thin
golden link necklace, seems very old.  The hinges on it are coming a bit loose,
but it's still pretty tightly closed.$d$),
  (584, 9, $d$The woman in this painting is amazingly beautiful, but in the same
way that a deadly sword is beautiful. She's exactly like a sword --
whipcord-lithe, slender, well-muscled, and seems as if she is about
to strike. Her eyes seem incredibly intelligent and perceptive. The
portrait is no bigger than the palm of your hand, making the artistry
of the representation seem all the more amazing.
   The woman in the painting is looking right out at the viewer. As
you watch, her full, lush lips move, and you hear words: "My little
Frederick, remember that I am always watching over you." You hear no
more.$d$, $d$The woman in this painting is amazingly beautiful, but in the same
way that a deadly sword is beautiful. She's exactly like a sword --
whipcord-lithe, slender, well-muscled, and seems as if she is about
to strike. Her eyes seem incredibly intelligent and perceptive. The
portrait is no bigger than the palm of your hand, making the artistry
of the representation seem all the more amazing.
   The woman in the painting is looking right out at the viewer. As
you watch, her full, lush lips move, and you hear words: "My little
Frederick, remember that I am always watching over you." You hear no
more.$d$),
  (584, 10, $d$This coat is made of long, narrow strips of cloth and leather sewn together
into a long-sleeved, heavy robe with inlaid armholes.  The cloth is red, blue,
and purple velvet, alternating with black leather.  When you put it on, your
head tingles with new ideas and the residue of dreams, making you feel a little
wild-eyed.$d$, $d$This coat is made of long, narrow strips of cloth and leather sewn together
into a long-sleeved, heavy robe with inlaid armholes.  The cloth is red, blue,
and purple velvet, alternating with black leather.  When you put it on, your
head tingles with new ideas and the residue of dreams, making you feel a little
wild-eyed.$d$),
  (584, 11, $d$This desk is hand-made, and seems very old. A traditional rolltop desk
with lots of room to write letters on, it has a multitude of little
drawers. One in particular feels a bit loose.$d$, $d$This desk is hand-made, and seems very old. A traditional rolltop desk
with lots of room to write letters on, it has a multitude of little
drawers. One in particular feels a bit loose.$d$),
  (584, 12, $d$The book is leatherbound. It's quite old, obviously. When you open it,
a cloud of fine dust flies up, tickling your nose and stinging your eyes.
Each of the yellowed, crumbling pages is written in the same crabbed,
faltering handwriting. It's quite difficult to read, but you puzzle it
out slowly. A Table of Contents says that the thin volume contains five
separate letters. It is divided into sections by a beautiful coloured
painting bound right into the book.
  You can look at section1, section2, section3, section4, or section5.$d$, $d$The book is leatherbound. It's quite old, obviously. When you open it,
a cloud of fine dust flies up, tickling your nose and stinging your eyes.
Each of the yellowed, crumbling pages is written in the same crabbed,
faltering handwriting. It's quite difficult to read, but you puzzle it
out slowly. A Table of Contents says that the thin volume contains five
separate letters. It is divided into sections by a beautiful coloured
painting bound right into the book.
  You can look at section1, section2, section3, section4, or section5.$d$),
  (584, 13, $d$This shield is made of bright blue-white steel, but it glows with a faint pink
aura.  The design on the front is ancient and very familiar, though you can't
immediately place it for now.  And if you put your ear against its softly
thrumming surface, you can hear what seems to be a lullaby, in a strong female
voice touched with gentleness.$d$, $d$This shield is made of bright blue-white steel, but it glows with a faint pink
aura.  The design on the front is ancient and very familiar, though you can't
immediately place it for now.  And if you put your ear against its softly
thrumming surface, you can hear what seems to be a lullaby, in a strong female
voice touched with gentleness.$d$),
  (584, 14, $d$This crown seems pretty heavy.  It's made of thick gold, and probably
incredibly expensive.  The gold is shaped into the traditional peaks of crowns.
A green emerald, marquise-cut, is set into each peak, and several of them in
various cuts adorn the very front of the crown's tallest peak, which would be
centered over the wearer's forehead.$d$, $d$This crown seems pretty heavy.  It's made of thick gold, and probably
incredibly expensive.  The gold is shaped into the traditional peaks of crowns.
A green emerald, marquise-cut, is set into each peak, and several of them in
various cuts adorn the very front of the crown's tallest peak, which would be
centered over the wearer's forehead.$d$),
  (584, 15, $d$The glowing pages glow with power, telling a story older than time itself --
that of gods and mortals, struggles with beasts greater than any the world has
ever known, true love and blackest hatred, friendship and betrayal..  All
couched in the language of ancient times to form a manual of behavior for
magicians in the aftermath of a war the likes of which may never be seen
again...  Though the majority of the ancient book's thick pages seem torn out
or damaged, enough of it remains for you to see that it must be very valuable.
The cover looks like a good place to start learning about this book.$d$, $d$The glowing pages glow with power, telling a story older than time itself --
that of gods and mortals, struggles with beasts greater than any the world has
ever known, true love and blackest hatred, friendship and betrayal..  All
couched in the language of ancient times to form a manual of behavior for
magicians in the aftermath of a war the likes of which may never be seen
again...  Though the majority of the ancient book's thick pages seem torn out
or damaged, enough of it remains for you to see that it must be very valuable.
The cover looks like a good place to start learning about this book.$d$),
  (584, 16, $d$The hood is purple leather, soft as silk, ornamented with golden ribbon around
the edges.  Its lappets hang down the wearer's chest and back, allowing the
hood to fall back.  An attendant air of disaster seems to hang around this
hood, but you must admit, it is very flattering.$d$, $d$The hood is purple leather, soft as silk, ornamented with golden ribbon around
the edges.  Its lappets hang down the wearer's chest and back, allowing the
hood to fall back.  An attendant air of disaster seems to hang around this
hood, but you must admit, it is very flattering.$d$),
  (584, 17, $d$This beautiful cloak is made of some kind of silky white fabric sewn all over
with the most amazing white feathers.  Each full, white feather has a single
dark blue dot near its tip, giving the cloak a kind of shimmery nature as it
turns from white to dappled.  The cloak fits closely about its wearer's body,
with a white leather clasp holding it closed at the throat and at the waist.$d$, $d$This beautiful cloak is made of some kind of silky white fabric sewn all over
with the most amazing white feathers.  Each full, white feather has a single
dark blue dot near its tip, giving the cloak a kind of shimmery nature as it
turns from white to dappled.  The cloak fits closely about its wearer's body,
with a white leather clasp holding it closed at the throat and at the waist.$d$),
  (584, 18, $d$These wings look so real!  A metallic golden frame supports two somewhat large
wings made of some kind of silk that stretches to the point of being almost
transparent.  Some kind of sparkly things are woven into the silk, making the
wings shimmer as they move.$d$, $d$These wings look so real!  A metallic golden frame supports two somewhat large
wings made of some kind of silk that stretches to the point of being almost
transparent.  Some kind of sparkly things are woven into the silk, making the
wings shimmer as they move.$d$),
  (584, 19, $d$The scythe's blade is about the length of a human's leg, curved inward and
polished to a shine.  It's mounted onto a wooden shaft about the same length as
the blade.  Overall, it's a gruesome weapon.$d$, $d$The scythe's blade is about the length of a human's leg, curved inward and
polished to a shine.  It's mounted onto a wooden shaft about the same length as
the blade.  Overall, it's a gruesome weapon.$d$),
  (584, 20, $d$This sword's easily the length of your entire arm, and the blade itself is
thick and wide, with a blood groove deeply etched into its center.  It's
clearly incredibly old.  You just can't find this kind of workmanship these
days.$d$, $d$This sword's easily the length of your entire arm, and the blade itself is
thick and wide, with a blood groove deeply etched into its center.  It's
clearly incredibly old.  You just can't find this kind of workmanship these
days.$d$),
  (584, 21, $d$How disgusting! This bit of slick leathery fish bulges slightly, from
whatever its previous owner ate just before they parted ways. It smells
absolutely foul.$d$, $d$How disgusting! This bit of slick leathery fish bulges slightly, from
whatever its previous owner ate just before they parted ways. It smells
absolutely foul.$d$),
  (584, 22, $d$A pity you can't read anything on this paper. It's written
