  (584, 31, $d$You see a loose belt made of braided wildflowers.  The daisies and honeysuckles
were connected by threading each flower through its neighbor somehow.  They
must be enchanted, for you cannot separate any of the flowers from the belt.$d$, $d$You see a loose belt made of braided wildflowers.  The daisies and honeysuckles
were connected by threading each flower through its neighbor somehow.  They
must be enchanted, for you cannot separate any of the flowers from the belt.$d$),
  (584, 32, $d$You can see that this girth must be not only magical, but intrinsically strong,
for though it is very old, there are no dents, dings, or scratches in its
shockingly blue surface.  It reflects a fierce strike of lightning as you look
at it.  But no lightning flashed right then in the sky....$d$, $d$You can see that this girth must be not only magical, but intrinsically strong,
for though it is very old, there are no dents, dings, or scratches in its
shockingly blue surface.  It reflects a fierce strike of lightning as you look
at it.  But no lightning flashed right then in the sky....$d$),
  (584, 33, $d$You can tell that only royalty could have afforded to make these.  Made of some
dark-green metal alloy, these bracers, made to fit and buckle around a very
large arm, are worked in a cunning scrolling design.  They're obviously very
old, as well; the metal feels worn in places, as though decades of contact with
the same arms have altered their shape slightly.$d$, $d$You can tell that only royalty could have afforded to make these.  Made of some
dark-green metal alloy, these bracers, made to fit and buckle around a very
large arm, are worked in a cunning scrolling design.  They're obviously very
old, as well; the metal feels worn in places, as though decades of contact with
the same arms have altered their shape slightly.$d$),
  (584, 34, $d$This very old shackle's made of steel.  There are numerous little dents in its
surface, but it still seems supernaturally strong.  It fastens with a steel
clip.$d$, $d$This very old shackle's made of steel.  There are numerous little dents in its
surface, but it still seems supernaturally strong.  It fastens with a steel
clip.$d$),
  (584, 35, $d$These papers seem to be a deed of some sort.  As you read on you notice a large
sum of money was paid to a merchant for the purchase of a young blond haired
maiden.  This paper entitles the bearer of this deed, ownership to the
aforementioned maiden.$d$, $d$These papers seem to be a deed of some sort.  As you read on you notice a large
sum of money was paid to a merchant for the purchase of a young blond haired
maiden.  This paper entitles the bearer of this deed, ownership to the
aforementioned maiden.$d$),
  (584, 36, $d$Legends tell of times when the veil between the worlds grows thin and small
slivers of what exists beyond the penumbra slip into the mortal realm.  In the
most miraculous of instances, these slivers crystallize and form objects known
as "Dreamshards."

As a manifestation of the collective unconscious, this dagger is a testament to
the power of wonder and hope.  It scintillates with the inner light of the
stuff of dreams themselves.$d$, $d$Legends tell of times when the veil between the worlds grows thin and small
slivers of what exists beyond the penumbra slip into the mortal realm.  In the
most miraculous of instances, these slivers crystallize and form objects known
as "Dreamshards."

As a manifestation of the collective unconscious, this dagger is a testament to
the power of wonder and hope.  It scintillates with the inner light of the
stuff of dreams themselves.$d$),
  (584, 92, $d$Ewww! How disgusting! It's made of the ribs of a dead chicken. The bones
