  (587, 1, $d$It's made of polished cream-grey stones cobbled together into
a cylindrical shape. Though it's not very large, it's probably
more than able to handle the water demands of the compound it
calls home. When you lean over and look inside it, you can
see sparkling water far below.$d$, $d$It's made of polished cream-grey stones cobbled together into
a cylindrical shape. Though it's not very large, it's probably
more than able to handle the water demands of the compound it
calls home. When you lean over and look inside it, you can
see sparkling water far below.$d$),
  (587, 2, $d$You behold a simple circular shape held rigid with boiled leather
straps that support some kind of oiled canvas that probably holds
water. A stopper on the canteen's mouth keeps the liquid inside
