the dried on blood that forms the outer layer of the earring.$d$),
  (590, 3, $d$The sword feels light in your hands as you inspect it.  There are many
scratches and dents in it, but it remains razor sharp to the touch.  The
gleaming metal that it has been forged from is superior to most other materials
used for swords.  The handle is layered in gold and silver, with very detailed
designs of ivy leaves.  There is an inscription on the handle.$d$, $d$The sword feels light in your hands as you inspect it.  There are many
scratches and dents in it, but it remains razor sharp to the touch.  The
gleaming metal that it has been forged from is superior to most other materials
used for swords.  The handle is layered in gold and silver, with very detailed
designs of ivy leaves.  There is an inscription on the handle.$d$),
  (590, 4, $d$   The rusted key is flaking off metal in spots, giving it a very rough feel.
The wooden handle is cracked and splintered, as if the key has seen a lot of
use.$d$, $d$   The rusted key is flaking off metal in spots, giving it a very rough feel.
The wooden handle is cracked and splintered, as if the key has seen a lot of
