  (590, 5, $d$   The key is carved of a dull grey stone, and seems to be well worn at the
edges.  It is rather large and heavy, being that it is made from stone.$d$, $d$   The key is carved of a dull grey stone, and seems to be well worn at the
edges.  It is rather large and heavy, being that it is made from stone.$d$),
  (590, 6, $d$The worn out leather book binding is almost falling apart.  It is very old
and the leather is well oiled from being handed by unclean hands.  The pages in
the book are hand written with a variety of inks giving light to the idea that
the pages were written on different days as if a journal would be.  You can
read a few of the first pages: page1, page2 and page3.$d$, $d$The worn out leather book binding is almost falling apart.  It is very old
and the leather is well oiled from being handed by unclean hands.  The pages in
