  (11, 22, ARRAY['iron-helm', 'small']::text[], $d$This simple little iron helm is made almost completely without ornamentation,
aside from very simple tooling along its edge.  Leather straps hold it onto its
wearer's head.  It's also quite heavy and probably very hot!$d$),
  (12, 44, ARRAY['pants', 'fur', 'wolf']::text[], $d$These pants are made of grey wolf fur.  The are sized to fit a giant, and they
must have come from a huge wolf.$d$),
  (12, 45, ARRAY['poem', 'riddle']::text[], $d$A special Valentine's game for you
To see if your heart is pure and true
Two items you'll need to finish the game
Two different ones, mind, not two of the same
The first is a pink rose of friendship and love
The next is a box with sweet treats from above
The rose can be found on ones who love true
A young Queen whose domain is really quite new
A man who loves one of royalty's blood
And a mother of pink on all fours with her brood
And do not forget the one who loves roses
And all other plants be they ravens or posies
The poem continues on part2.$d$),
  (12, 45, ARRAY['part2']::text[], $d$For the box you will have to go farther afield
For one is on someone who holds a pink shield
The next two wear rings of eternal devotion
Though one is a Bride's and the other one broken
The last box is on a bird full of desire
His heart is too hot to touch; it's all fire
Once you have both you will know what to do
This riddle can only be finished with two
From what's in the box you should bring them to me
And perhaps a return of the prisoner you'll see$d$),
  (12, 46, ARRAY['rune']::text[], $d$The silver rune is printed on the velvet in an unfamiliar script, but in very
small letters below it the word "Love" is written in common.$d$),
  (12, 66, ARRAY['symbol']::text[], $d$An eye with three eyebrows and a tear is dyed on with blue and
purple dye.$d$),
