  (30, 111, ARRAY['page1']::text[], $d$Hey! diddle, diddle,
  The child wrote a scribble,
The sun hopped over the stream;
The big dragon laughed petting his gems,
And the teapot began to steam!

The nursery rhymes continue on page2.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page2']::text[], $d$Wug the Fi'ry Drakling, lived in the fields
And frolicked with the tomatoes 'til he got bashed down with shields!
Little newbies always killed that rascal Wug
And brought him hell and suffering and crushed him like a bug!

The nursery rhymes continue on page3.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page3']::text[], $d$There once was a rogue from Mielikki
Who told all his friends he was sneaky
So he went to a cave
And was feeling quite brave
But now Mysa has a new toy rogue squeaky

The nursery rhymes continue on page4.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page4']::text[], $d$Glug and Gwill went up the hill
To burn a human city.
Glug fell down not far from the town
And Gwill wrote this little ditty.

The nursery rhymes continue on page5.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page5']::text[], $d$Little Mage Bigby sat in the corner,
Hoping he wouldn't be missed.
He cast with his hand a spell oh so grand,
And thus we have Bigby's Clenched Fist.

The nursery rhymes continue on page6.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page6']::text[], $d$Cast, cast, cast the spell,
Quickly and with skill.
Daintily, cautiously, gracefully, carefully,
Magic's but a drill.

The nursery rhymes continue on page7.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page7']::text[], $d$It'sa pixie time
They steals the sticks-y twine
A little mouse
Caught in a house
Now he's pickled in brine!

The nursery rhymes continue on page8.$d$),
  (30, 111, ARRAY['page8']::text[], $d$Take their ears
Pee in their beers
It's all in fun
Now sing of their fears$d$),
  (30, 299, ARRAY['dedication']::text[], $d$   Those missed are never forgotten when holding their memory in thy heart.
This memorial dedicated to Rick L Sala II.  Born: June 1, 1974.  Died: June 21,
2006.  Beloved brother, friend, mentor, deity, husband, and father.  Rick our
dearest of friends, Brother may rest among the Garden of Eden in peace.

Daroowise Ap Nuatha
Pergus Tynllyr$d$),
  (30, 303, ARRAY['tip', 'tips']::text[], $d$Type one of the following:
   Look commands
   Look fights
   Look leveling
   Look renting
   Look rules
   Look map
   Look closing$d$),
  (30, 303, ARRAY['commands', 'command']::text[], $d$Before you get started in your adventures, we ask that you do a little
reading to help you understand Fiery's environment and how things work.
Please be patient, reading all of this should take you less then
5 minutes.

Here are a few of things we strongly advise you to read, type:
HELP -> A list of all the major commands.
HELP NEWBIE -> Brief newbie advice on areas to try.
HELP RULES -> A listing of Fiery Mud's rules.
HELP AREAS -> A list of current areas and their respective levels.
HELP KILLER -> A brief warning about attacking players.
HELP 100 -> A list of the limitations for immortals and gods.
NEWS -> A list of all the mud's changes <Not necessary to read immediately>.$d$),
  (30, 303, ARRAY['fights', 'fight']::text[], $d$After you've read the rules, you might feel the urge to KILL something.
There's a large field just outside the west gate that's pretty safe,
especially if you first CONSIDER the creatures you want to kill.
Killing creatures will earn you experience points, and sometimes gold.
Remember that you can GET ALL from the corpse, and TAP the corpse when
you're done, to tidy things up.$d$),
  (30, 303, ARRAY['leveling', 'levels', 'level']::text[], $d$Try typing SCORE. When you have earned enough experience points, you will
be ready to level. This is done at your guild, by typing LEVEL GAIN. It
might be a good idea to visit your guild right away, for this is also the
place where you can PRACTICE new skills or spells. Guilds can be found
close to the town center. Monks and Rangers can level at the Warrior's
Guild. All the other classes must level in their respective guilds.$d$),
  (30, 303, ARRAY['renting', 'rent', 'quitting', 'quit']::text[], $d$Should you get hungry, there's a bakery on North Commerce Avenue.  There are
also many other ways of creating and/or finding food about the realm.
Currently renting at the inn is free, with a limit on 50 items per player to
reduce any problems that could occur.  To view your current load you may use
the offer command at the inn.  Camping is also another alternative, and can be
done in any outdoors room.  It is free, and allows you to stay far away from
town if you haven't completed your current adventure.  Typing QUIT is possible
but NOT something you should generally do, for you will lose all of your
equipment.$d$),
  (30, 303, ARRAY['rules']::text[], $d$FieryMud has a few simple rules. For a fairly complete listing of rules,
type: h rules -- but be aware that this list can change without notice.
ALL PLAYERS are expected to know the rules.

  You should definitely read the altar board for more information, as well
as the news, at some point. All players are expected to know what is
contained therein!$d$),
