  (63, 8, ARRAY['gloves', 'dragon', 'hide', 'dragon-hide', 'pair', 'a-pair-of-dragon-hide-gloves', 'venath']::text[], $d$Though they are indeed solid brown leather, these gloves appear to be covered
in thick smoke which eminates from the pores of the leathery surface.  The
effect of the distortion from the smoke is akin to a heatwave passing through
the desert.  Although by appearances they should offer little in the way of
protection, these gloves boast the strength and resiliance of the dragon whose
skin they were crafted from.  There appears to be an inscription on the inside
of the right hand glove.$d$),
  (63, 8, ARRAY['inscription']::text[], $d$Emblazoned in the leather on the inside of the cuff reads:
Specially crafted for the legendary assassin Kresselack, may his stiletto's forever haunt his foes.$d$),
  (64, 5, ARRAY['ruby']::text[], $d$The gold amulet's ruby is immaculate, and much larger than the average jewel.
It seems to glow with an inner warmth.  As you look into its center, words fill
your thoughts...

...the Shiori was once an order of the pyromantic arts which was dedicated to
the understanding and furtherment of magic.  The Prime Shior was the greatest
of these mages, and the head of the Kerristone-based order.  But even he could
not escape the Great Crash, and he perished along with the others whom the gods
deemed infidels.  As the Towers of Shiori fell upon him, he flung his amulet
through time itself, such that the Shiori legacy might not be forgotten...$d$),
  (83, 26, ARRAY['corpse', 'injoni', 'rif', 'decayed']::text[], $d$Wrapped in some sort of paper material, the oldest and first Frakati lies here
in silent peace.  This man lead his people through the thick woods of the
surrounding land, and started the first Frakati settlement.  A strong and
powerful warrior, the corpse of this long deceased hero lies here, eternally
guarded by the largest Frakati warrior you've ever seen.$d$),
  (86, 1, ARRAY['inscription']::text[], $d$The inscription reads:
To the MeerCat people, I owe my life to you. Although I can never hope to
repay that debt, I hope this fountain will quench the thirst of you and your
children for generations to come. I shall never forget your hospitality.
-Beraak$d$),
  (103, 16, ARRAY['insignia']::text[], $d$The symbol is that of a single red feather slanting diagonally against a
snowflake.$d$),
  (103, 17, ARRAY['insignia']::text[], $d$The symbol is that of a single red feather slanting diagonally against a
snowflake.$d$),
