  (188, 50, ARRAY['page3']::text[], $d$This Draconium catalogues the species of dragons represented in the
Duclian senate at the time of writing, the 11th Day of the Month of
Revolution, 14 MIE.  It magically updates itself, listing only the
species of dragons surviving.

The dragons are separated into three major groups based on alignment,
and each of these further divided into two groups each, the true dragons
and the supplementals.  For the first three sections, each page
describes one species of dragon, listing their alignment, type, average
length, breath weapon, any unique spells or skills they might exhibit,
whether they have the ability to shapeshift, and their relative strength
index.

The relative strength index is a device the Duclian Organizational Force
uses to rank species' relative powers.  It is only an average estimate.
These lesser races of the Creator are estimated to rank between zero and
ten, but no higher.

The final section of this catalogue details the powers and effects of
breath weapons, special skills, and draconian-specific spells.  The
appendicies also contains a page that will magically renew itself,
always reading the names of the current leaders of each draconian
faction.  At the time of this writing, the great 27 Senator Dragons are
listed.

                           Avahern the Chronicler
                           Royal Library of Duclia$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page5']::text[], $d$    The Dragons of Good

       The Metallic
 7.      Gold
 8.      Silver
 9.      Bronze
 10.     Brass
 11.     Copper
       The Ferric
 12.     Iron
 13.     Steel-Blue$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page7']::text[], $d$================================ <b:yellow>Gold</> ================================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        metallic
  Length:                      30-50 meters
  Breath weapon:               fire
  Unique spells:               deadly screech
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     81

  The strongest of the metallics, golden dragons are well known as
  champions of purity and justice.  They are typically friendly
  creatures, exhibiting pronounced benevolence.  Gold dragons are
  known to live in any habitat, adapting quickly and easily.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page8']::text[], $d$=============================== <b>Silver</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        metallic
  Length:                      25-40 meters
  Breath weapon:               frost
  Unique spells:               metallurgy
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     70

  Kind and magnanimous, silver dragons enjoy helping those weaker
  than themselves.  Silvers can often be found amongst the company
  of humans and elves.  Flying is a true pleasure to silvers,
  reflected by their preference of lofty mountain peaks for homes.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page9']::text[], $d$=============================== <yellow>Bronze</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        metallic
  Length:                      25-35 meters
  Breath weapon:               lightning
  Unique spells:               reconstitution
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     58

  Bronze dragons are partial to deep water, enjoying aquatic food
  and company.  They are adept swimmers, able to travel nearly as
  fast underwater as airborne.  Justice is important to bronze
  dragons, who do not tolerate cruelty or anarchy at all.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page10']::text[], $d$=============================== <yellow>Brass</> ================================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        metallic
  Length:                      20-30 meters
  Breath weapon:               gas
  Unique spells:               hand of transport
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     55

  Oddly, brass dragons are the most social of all dragons, even
  though they typically choose deserts to inhabit.  Some brass
  dragons will confine visitors only to keep them around longer to
  talk.  Sunlight and dry heat are especially pleasing to them.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page11']::text[], $d$=============================== <yellow>Copper</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        metallic
  Length:                      15-25 meters
  Breath weapon:               acid
  Unique spells:               defamation
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     45

  Copper dragons have well-deserved reputations as pranksters,
  jokers, and riddlers, often staying out of the reach of opponents
  while shouting insults and abuses.  They are the most selfish and
  greedy of the good dragons.  Coppers often lair in dry mountain or
  hill caves.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page12']::text[], $d$================================ <b:black>Iron</> ================================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        ferric
  Length:                      25-35 meters
  Breath weapon:               acid
  Unique spells:               iron maiden
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     59

  Iron dragons' personalities usually match their steely hides,
  making them appear cold and unresponsive.  Nevertheless, they are
  strong-willed warriors of righteousness who never give up.  Their
  lairs are usually deep subterranean caves or abandoned mines.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page13']::text[], $d$============================= <b>Steel</>-<blue>Blue</> =============================

  Alignment:                   good
  Type:                        ferric
  Length:                      30-35 meters
  Breath weapon:               lightning
  Unique spells:               bodily charge
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     64

  Even more inflexible and relentless than their iron dragon cousins,
  steel dragons follow rigorous schedules and procedures, making
  excellent soldiers.  For their size, they are quite powerful,
  reflected by continual static crackling about their bodies.  Most
  steel-blue dragons lair in mountain caves.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page15']::text[], $d$    The Neutral Dragons

       The Crystalline
 17.     Amethyst
 18.     Sapphire
 19.     Emerald
 20.     Topaz
 21.     Crystal
       The Elemental
 22.     Cloud
 23.     Mercury$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page17']::text[], $d$============================== <b:magenta>Amethyst</> ==============================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        crystalline
  Length:                      40-50 meters
  Breath weapon:               psionic
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               hypnosis
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     85

  Perhaps the most beautiful of all, amethyst dragons are also wiser
  than most.  They dislike conflict, and may even use their hypnotic
  abilities to prevent or stop combat.  Amethyst dragons are most
  likely found by remote mountainous lakes.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page18']::text[], $d$============================== <b:blue>Sapphire</> ==============================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        crystalline
  Length:                      30-40 meters
  Breath weapon:               sonicboom
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     72

  Sapphire dragons are very territorial, quickly attacking intruders
  on their stomping grounds without asking questions first.  This
  trait is aided by their ability to fly extremely fast and their
  superior hearing.  They typically live deep underground in
  self-constructed burrows.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page19']::text[], $d$=============================== <b:green>Emerald</> ==============================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        crystalline
  Length:                      20-35 meters
  Breath weapon:               shockwave
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     64

  Paranoid about the safety of their treasure, emerald dragons have
  multiple traps and alarms about their lair, which are often in
  dormant volcanoes.  As such, they are extremely heat resistant,
  and often shrug off a fireball as a gnat.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page20']::text[], $d$================================ <b:yellow>Topaz</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        crystalline
  Length:                      15-30 meters
  Breath weapon:               dehydration
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     53

  Topaz dragons are unfriendly solitary creatures, disliking any
  kind of company, human or dragon.  They often lair near the sea,
  but have a slight aversion to the water, reflected even in their
  breath weapon.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page21']::text[], $d$================================ <b:white>Crystal</> ================================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        crystalline
  Length:                      10-25 meters
  Breath weapon:               light
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     43

  The smallest of the gemstone dragons, crystal dragons are friendly
  and curious.  They lair in colder climates, where the skies are
  clearer, because they enjoy stargazing.  Crystal dragons have been
  known to adopt baby white dragons.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page22']::text[], $d$=============================== <b:cyan>Cloud</> ================================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        elemental
  Length:                      40-60 meters
  Breath weapon:               lightning, frost
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     89

  The largest of the neutral dragons, cloud dragons always lair in
  the clouds, the ability to turn themselves into a misty cloud
  allowing them to float effortlessly through the air.  Beginning as
  a whitish silver hue at birth, their scales slowly shift to muted
  sunset reds, oranges, and violets as they age.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page23']::text[], $d$============================== <b:black>Mercury</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   neutral
  Type:                        elemental
  Length:                      20-35 meters
  Breath weapon:               gas
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               <none>
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     58

  Mercury dragons have shiny hides, flowing liquid mercury making up
  their entire bodies.  They can harden or liquify at will, changing
  shape to anything, though they maintain their shiny appearance.
  These dragons are unpredictible and solitary, living in caves.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page25']::text[], $d$    The Dragons of Evil

       The Chromatic
 27.     Black
 28.     Red
 29.     Green
 30.     Blue
 31.     White
       The Nebulous
 32.     Shadow
 33.     Silver-Black$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page27']::text[], $d$================================ <b:black>Black</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        chromatic
  Length:                      25-50 meters
  Breath weapon:               acid
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               pounce
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     81

  Usually lairing in swamps and jungles, black dragon's dark color
  helps them camoflague themselves.  As excellent swimmers, they
  subsist on an aquatic diet.  They are abusive, self-absorbed,
  and power-hungry, abandoning children and allies to save
  themselves.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page28']::text[], $d$================================= <red>Red</> ================================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        chromatic
  Length:                      35-45 meters
  Breath weapon:               fire
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               claw
  Shapeshifter:                yes
  Relative Strength Index:     75

  Red dragons are extremely greedy, arrogant, and vain, considering
  themselves superior to just about everything.  Many red dragons
  are obsessed with amassing their treasure hordes.  They are both
  exceptionally intelligent and fiercely territorial, living in
  temperate to arid hills and mountains.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page29']::text[], $d$================================ <green>Green</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        chromatic
  Length:                      25-35 meters
  Breath weapon:               gas
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               pound
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     60

  Green dragons are foul-tempered creatures, living in forests and
  regularly enslaving any woodland races in their territory with
  cruelty.  Usually solitary, green dragons, are nevertheless very
  protective of their young, fighting to the death for their safety.
  Cunning and crafty, green dragons concoct elaborate schemes to
  ruin their opponents, rather than attacking overtly.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page30']::text[], $d$================================ <blue>Blue</> ================================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        chromatic
  Length:                      20-30 meters
  Breath weapon:               lightning
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               sonicboom
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     55

  Like the other chromatic dragons, blue dragons are extremely
  territorial, living in arid deserts where they can easily see
  long distances across their territory.  The sands keep their
  scales polished and glossy all their life.  Blue dragons are
  lawful evil.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page31']::text[], $d$================================ <b:white>White</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        chromatic
  Length:                      15-25 meters
  Breath weapon:               frost
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               snow
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     43

  The smallest and least intelligent of the chromatic dragons, white
  dragons live exclusively in cold places, especially icy and snowy
  locations.  White dragons are foolhardy and vicious, ripping their
  opponents to shreds before devouring them.  They like their food
  crunchy and frozen.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page32']::text[], $d$=============================== <b:black>Shadow</> ===============================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        nebulous
  Length:                      30-40 meters
  Breath weapon:               <none>
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               shadow
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     71

  Zombie-like and passive, shadow dragons rely entirely on instinct.
  With no higher intelligence, they are common targets for liches
  and psionics bent on world domination.  They are well-designed for
  combat, for whatever instinct they have seems to make them agile
  and vicious combatants.  Shadow dragons have the ability to turn
  themselves into massless shadows, immune from physical attacks.$d$),
  (188, 50, ARRAY['page33']::text[], $d$============================ <b>Silver</>-<b:black>Black</> ============================

  Alignment:                   evil
  Type:                        nebulous
  Length:                      15-30 meters
  Breath weapon:               acid, lightning
  Unique spells:               <none>
  Unique skills:               hypnosis
  Shapeshifter:                no
  Relative Strength Index:     50

  Believed by some to be a bastard breed between black and silver
  dragons, in truth silver-black dragons are a rare species all
  their own.  They are fierce and extremely intelligent fighters,
  always anxious to inflate their pride.  They are not indigenous
  to Caelia, and have been known to attack Nymrill and Dheduu.$d$),
