  (464, 0, ARRAY['carving', 'woman', 'circular']::text[], $d$     The carving appears to be an image of the goddess Selina.  The sculpture
is surprisingly intricate, detailed so much so that you wonder what master
craftsman captured her beauty and essence so in such a simple medium.
     The scene rendered shows the goddess at home in her Waterfall Grotto.
Seeing her home you can easily comprehend her love of all things of nature; it is
of little wonder that she should touch the Aviary with her grace and grant the
citizens of the bleak north a respite from winter's grasp within these walls.$d$),
  (464, 0, ARRAY['water']::text[], $d$     The water spurts from the uppermost basin to first fill it and then flow
down through a series of bowls, pools, and basins until it pours into a swift
brook that moves off to the west.  The water is crystal-clear and refreshingly
crisp to the touch, likely melted ice from beyond the walls of the aviary.  The
liquid reminds you of your dry throat; surely the birds would not mind if you
took a small drink from one of the sparkling basins.$d$),
  (464, 3, ARRAY['inscription', 'handle']::text[], $d$
Mielikki Topiary Gardenworks$d$),
  (480, 19, ARRAY['carving', 'carvings']::text[], $d$The carvings seem to show a group of people vanishing from one room and
appearing in another.$d$),
  (480, 28, ARRAY['writing', 'wall']::text[], $d$The writing reads, "Gaze upon those that have opposed me and know that I
am supreme."$d$),
